# SVC Lab Neural Processing Project

A collection of hardware designs, neural-network models, RTL implementations, and FPGA projects developed by the SVC Lab.

## Repository Structure

| Directory | Description |
|---|---|
| `systolic/` | Proposed systolic-array architecture and related design files |
| `uart/` | UART modules for testing the proposed designs on FPGA hardware |
| `RO-TRNG/` | Ring Oscillator–based True Random Number Generator design |
| `NNmodel/` | Neural-network models and their RTL implementations |
| `FPGA/` | FPGA implementation files, constraints, and project resources |

## Required Tools

The following tools are required for simulation, synthesis, and FPGA implementation:

- [Icarus Verilog](https://steveicarus.github.io/iverilog/)
- [Verilator](https://www.veripool.org/verilator/)
- [Yosys](https://yosyshq.net/yosys/)
- [AMD Vivado Design Suite](https://www.amd.com/en/products/software/adaptive-socs-and-fpgas/vivado.html)

> Vivado is required only for FPGA synthesis, implementation, and bitstream generation.

## Supported FPGA Boards

### Nexys A7-100T

- FPGA: AMD Artix-7
- Device: `XC7A100T-1CSG324`
- Development environment: AMD Vivado Design Suite

### AXKU062

- FPGA: AMD Kintex UltraScale
- Device: `XCKU060-2FFVA1156I`
- Development environment: AMD Vivado Design Suite

